<title>JAPAN: Yasuda Trust to forgive 141 bln yen mortgage loans.</title>
<headline>Yasuda Trust to forgive 141 bln yen mortgage loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yasuda Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd said on Monday that it had decided to forgive loans worth 141.12 billion yen which it had extended to Juso Inc, one of the seven failed mortgage firms or &quot;jusen&quot; liquidated under a government scheme.  </p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that the loan forgiveness had already been taken into account in its earnings forecast for the current year to March 31, 1997, which it announced in May.</p>
